{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From his ways he is sated</b> — It stands in place of two. Form is pa'al on the pattern of מול, and its meaning is 'turn aside,' and דעת is read לב. And likewise the interpretation: from his ways — which are the ways of futility — from them a man is sated, and the form is מדעת, for HaShem sates him with the reward of his deeds and feeds him the fruit of his ways." "<b>And from its boughs</b> — from the ascending of the olive. He likened his good deeds, the light commandments, to the leaves and the weighty ones to the fruit. And likewise: he is sated even from the leaf, a good man; and 'sated' is the reward of the good deed." "Another interpretation: <b>מעליו</b> — from himself."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:45.926352356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}